  "notebook": {
    "cellContents": {
      "d0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "d0000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# Syrup Value Type as Categorical Schema\n\nThe OCapN Syrup serialization format's recursive Value union, expressed as a schema (category with attributes). Objects are Syrup types; morphisms encode containment/reference relationships.\n\nThis schema is the **grammar** that constrains tree diffusion. Every intermediate state during denoising must be a valid instance of this schema. The five diffusion approaches (A-E) all operate on instances of this schema.\n\n## Connection to Tree Diffusion (Berkeley ICLR 2025)\n- Forward noise: grammar-constrained subtree replacement within Value tree\n- Reverse denoise: learned neural policy predicts (position, replacement) pairs\n- TreeDiff: O(|A|+|B|) edit paths between Value instances\n- CFG constraint: Syrup grammar ensures 100% syntactic validity at every step\n\n## Connection to ncreel\n- ReelState is an instance of this schema\n- Each tablet's content is a nested Value subtree\n- The encoding: <<'reel:state' focused_idx [tablets...] {layout...}>>"
      },
